  "legend": {
   "x": 5200,
   "y": 13560,
   "w": 620,
   "maxH": 1100,
   "size": 24,
   "fill": "gray",
   "text": "How to read these boards\n\nGrey mono tag “Proposed component: …” = a composite built only from shadcn/ui parts and design-system components. It is not in the design system yet; the Proposed components board lists each one with its parts, for the owner to approve.\n\nBlue mono tag “Needs API: …” = the contract does not return this yet. Shown so the design can be judged; it must not ship as real data. “Live only” = it comes from a WebSocket event and is gone after a refresh.\n\nLayout (owner decision): the page never scrolls. New orders live in a persistent strip in the header, under the app bar (owner decision), every Accept in view; the list of orders in progress is a virtualised grid that scrolls inside itself; detail opens in an in-page panel beside it, and the timeline in a third pane. No dialogs for working tasks: decline, confirmations and screen health all open in the page. The only blocking dialog is “signed out”.\n\nLaunch scope: no package seals (next version): the kitchen reads a pickup code to the rider, who types it in (owner decision). Light theme only, one owner login per restaurant (no staff), no Add delay, no notifications bell (later versions). Marking items out of stock is in launch (owner decision): declining for an unavailable item offers it. No note with an acceptance (owner decision). Times are 12-hour (owner decision).\n\nMoney shown is what the API returns: You earn / Order net = restaurant_net_cents; commission shows commission_cents with no rate. Orange is only for accepting a new order; Mark ready is the forest button.\n\nCountdowns are live and loop so each board stays in its state. Every screen comes from the LiveBoard component; change its Scenario tweak to see any state."
  }
 },
